* {{Timeline-event |date={{Start date|1950}}|event=[[Alan Turing]] shows the word problem for [[cancellation semigroup]]s is unsolvable,<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Turing |first1=A. M. |title=The Word Problem in Semi-Groups With Cancellation |journal=[[The Annals of Mathematics]] |date=September 1950 |volume=52 |issue=2 |pages=491–505 |doi=10.2307/1969481|jstor=1969481 }}</ref> by furthering Post's construction. The proof is difficult to follow but marks a turning point in the word problem for groups.{{r|Miller|p=342}}}}
